A||||12||JSocha||Another baby "colt" born today for those interested...||||1||
Z||000000||JSocha||05-08-2001||03:31 PM||||Went home for lunch today, checked on our Mustang (who my wife checked on this morning before going to work) who has been expecting (overdue by two weeks) and we now have another baby boy.  Didn't have the camera for this one with me.<P>First colt was born 4-25-01 and was drinking water out of mama's bucket and munching on her hay the very same day.  Advanced colt and a strong little booger to boot!  Got this 5'11" 265 pound boy toppled over with just one trust of his little back legs when I was holding him.  Was an unexpected surprise to me I tell yah!<P>Two down, one mare to go...she should be due at about the end of May.<P>Did you hear that FieroLisa and Cammeron?  If interested, I will send pictures again.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Eric||05-08-2001||03:53 PM||||That's gross.  I was tricked into watching a horse give birth once.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Black88GT||05-08-2001||04:37 PM||||We had all of our foals born in March.  There not mine of course I just work there.  My boss decided to go to Aspen for a week and I had to watch the house (millionaire for a week hehe).  Keep in mind one of the mare's is already waxing up and is due any hour.  So he leaves anyway, me with tapes about how to deliver this thing.  They have camera's in the stall to watch for when she lays down, I was afraid to go to sleep.  Finally about 4 AM after watching some really bad late night movies (and some more of the instructional videos for safe measure), I see her lay down.  So I go out and it went pretty smoothly.  I did have to grab the foals legs and pull it out though.  Pretty interesting actually, kinda like the Discovery channel in real life.  I had the number of another vet (my boss is a vet.) to call so she could come over to make sure everything was OK.  It was but they had to stich up the foals eyelid or something, can't remember why.  <P>Now they are a couple months old and crazy as hell!  Soon we'll send them to the auction block in Kentucky and make my boss even more rich...||||reg||1
Z||000003||JSocha||05-08-2001||04:50 PM||||Quite the experience huh?<P>I was away (June of '95) for software training in MN when my Mustang had her first baby and after I had bought her.  Still have that Filly.<P>This is my wife's first time with babies even though she has been around horses most of her life.<P>The first one took a 1/2 hour which was to long, as I guess after their water breaks, they lay down and go into labor, 45 seconds later they poop the little ones out.  But what do I know...this is just what we have been told.<P>Hmmmmm?  Reminds me hearing about the Chezlavakian (or was it Russian) woman.  Out in a field one minute; pinching out a kid the next; and right back into the field right after giving birth.<P>GOSH Dats got to hurt!?!?!?!?!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroLisa||05-08-2001||05:14 PM||||Oh I just love foals! The mare at school gave birth to a colt last night, she should be back in about a week. <P>My mare on the other hand...... After $1,600 worth of training she's still not sellable. So I'm faced with the decision whether to throw more money into her. In July there will be a girl looking for "project horses" and I'm not necessarily looking for a lot of money for her so I gotta decide what to do. <BR>The gelding I was going to bring home for the summer very well might be sold on Thursday, and if hes gone I will probably cry! Some lady is coming to look at horses for her to re-train and shes looking at Brando (the guy I want) and Piper (who is all arounda  better horse) Brandos legs are all crooked, yet hes sound, so I'm hoping that will steer her away from him...Keep your fingers crossed, if he's not sold, I get to take him out cross country next week in my lesson.<P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 violet pearl 4 speed GT: 17 in. rims, lowered, cold-air intake<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<P><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A><P><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros/" TARGET=_blank>Tarheels Fieros Website</A>||||reg||1
